```
ROLE: area_chair
FINAL_VERDICT: yellow
REVIEWER_VOTES: {novelty_killer: yellow, systems_reviewer: yellow, evaluation_prosecutor: yellow, theory_skeptic: yellow, product_realist: green}
FATAL_OBJECTIONS: []
REQUIRED_EVIDENCE: [
  "1. ST .encode() vs .encode_query() direct comparison on arctic-embed-s: if ST's own .encode() auto-applies the default_prompt_name from config_sentence_transformers.json, the seam closes INSIDE SentenceTransformers and the wrapper-discard framing collapses entirely. This is the single most load-bearing untested assertion (theory_skeptic). Run: model.encode(queries) vs model.encode_query(queries) on arctic, report R@10 for each.",
  "2. In-situ end-to-end Chroma and/or pymilvus run: call collection.add() + collection.query() through the actual default SentenceTransformerEmbeddingFunction code path on SciFact with arctic-embed-s. Reproduce the A-number (~0.73 R@10) in situ. The L0 SIMULATES the wrapper discard via bare ST calls; the claim is about PRODUCTION WRAPPERS, so the gap must be demonstrated through them (evaluation_prosecutor, systems_reviewer).",
  "3. >=2 additional asymmetric-prompt self-describing models (e.g., Snowflake/snowflake-arctic-embed-m, BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5, or similar models that ship non-empty prompts in config_sentence_transformers.json). N=1 model means the effect-size variance ACROSS MODELS is undefined; the current CI is within-SciFact-arctic only (theory_skeptic).",
  "4. >=2 additional BEIR datasets (e.g., NFCorpus, FiQA, or TREC-COVID). SciFact is small (n=300 queries) and single-domain; effect may be domain-specific or scale-dependent (theory_skeptic, evaluation_prosecutor).",
  "5. Relabel framing: 'DISCARD' -> 'fail to auto-load by default'. All 4 wrappers EXPOSE prompt parameters (query_instruction, query_encode_kwargs, etc.) and merely default them empty. The accurate claim is 'wrappers do not auto-read the model artifact's shipped prompt contract,' not 'wrappers make it impossible to use prompts' (novelty_killer)."
]
MANDATORY_BASELINES: [
  "ST model.encode(queries) on arctic-embed-s (to isolate whether the seam is at ST boundary or wrapper boundary)",
  "Chroma default SentenceTransformerEmbeddingFunction end-to-end add()+query() with arctic-embed-s on SciFact",
  ">=1 additional self-describing model on SciFact to establish cross-model consistency",
  ">=1 additional BEIR dataset with arctic-embed-s to establish cross-dataset consistency"
]
MAP_DELTA_PROPOSAL: {node: "CLAIM-0061", change: "HOLD at L0-YELLOW. Do not advance to L1. Re-gate after REQUIRED_EVIDENCE items 1-4 are delivered. If item 1 shows ST .encode() auto-applies the config'd prompt (A_encode == B_encode_query), DOWNGRADE to RED and reclassify as known-mechanism-in-a-costume. If item 2 fails to reproduce the A-number in situ, DOWNGRADE to RED. If items 1-4 all support, re-convene committee for L1 gate with relabeled framing (item 5)."}
PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: yes
RATIONALE: Four of five reviewers vote YELLOW; product_realist votes GREEN. No RED votes, no fatal collisions, no unrebutted kills. The prior-art search is adequate: E5/Wang2022, Instructor/TART, ST v3 prompts/Router docs, and MTEB PR#1221 are all cited, and the claim honestly does NOT re-derive the prefix mechanism. The committee's consensus position is that the claim occupies a genuine but narrow delta on the INTEGRATION-DEFAULT axis, not the mechanism axis.

On killer #3 (known-mechanism-in-a-costume): the committee finds the discard-framing PARTIALLY distinct from "you forgot the prefix." Pre-ST-v3, there was no machine-readable prompt contract to discard — the user had to know the prefix from the model card. Post-v3, the model artifact self-describes (config_sentence_transformers.json) and ST auto-applies (encode_query/encode_document), so a competent user who picked a self-describing model and used the standard DB integration SHOULD expect it to work — yet it doesn't. That IS a distinct failure mode from "you didn't read the docs." However, the novelty_killer correctly identifies that wrappers EXPOSE prompt parameters (pymilvus: query_instruction, LangChain: query_encode_kwargs, LlamaIndex: query_instruction) and merely default them empty, so "DISCARD" overstates; "fail to auto-load" is accurate. This weakens the framing from "a silent, invisible failure" to "a bad default that a moderately diligent user could configure around." The delta survives but is modest — packaging/defaults, not mechanism.

On killer #9 (seam demonstrated open in production): 4 wrappers source-verified in code (2026-06-04). But the theory_skeptic raises a critical untested assumption: does ST's own .encode() method, when called by a wrapper on a v3+ model with populated prompts, auto-apply the default prompt? If yes, the wrappers are NOT discarding — ST's .encode() is doing the discarding, and the seam is inside ST, not at the wrapper boundary. This must be tested before the claim can advance. Additionally, the evaluation prosecutor correctly flags that the L0 only SIMULATES the wrapper discard; no actual Chroma/pymilvus end-to-end run has been executed. The claim is about production DB wrappers, so the measurement must pass through them.

The systems_reviewer notes vLLM already ships partial artifact-prompt loading (input_type), so "no production system does this" is false outside vector-DB wrappers — the strongest version of the claim is already weakened to a sector-specific (vector-DB) observation.

The L0 experimental controls are sound: alias-break (C ~ B) confirms the gain is from query prompt, not any-text; e5-small-v2 (A == B exactly) confirms effect vanishes on empty-prompt artifact. The reproduction is honest (pilot +10.3pp → indep +9.37pp R@10; R@1 rel gain 32% → 19.6% — reported, not hidden). But N=1 model, N=1 dataset, offline cosine NN (not ANN/HNSW) is too thin for advancement. The theory_skeptic correctly notes the paired-bootstrap CI is within-SciFact-arctic only; the cross-model and cross-dataset variance is undefined.

DECISION: YELLOW. The claim has genuine empirical substance and the controls are well-designed, but it cannot advance to L1 until: (1) the ST .encode() vs .encode_query() boundary is directly tested to confirm where the discard actually occurs, (2) the gap is reproduced in situ through an actual Chroma or pymilvus end-to-end call, (3) at least 2 more self-describing models and 2 more BEIR datasets establish generality, and (4) the framing is relabeled from "DISCARD" to "fail to auto-load by default" with all four prior-art cites front-and-center. If item (1) shows ST .encode() already auto-applies the prompt, the claim collapses to RED. PROMPT_VERSION=v001.
```
